    "text": "To determine the new salary of the secretary after a 2% increase, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the original salary.\n2. Calculate the amount of the salary increase.\n3. Add the increase to the original salary to find the new salary.\n\nStep 1: Identify the original salary.\nThe original salary is €10,000 per month.\n\nStep 2: Calculate the amount of the salary increase.\nThe salary increase is 2% of the original salary. To find 2% of €10,000, we multiply €10,000 by 0.02 (since 2% is equivalent to 0.02 in decimal form).\n\\[ \\text{Salary increase} = 10000 \\times 0.02 = 200 \\]\n\nStep 3: Add the increase to the original salary to find the new salary.\n\\[ \\text{New salary} = 10000 + 200 = 10200 \\]\n\nTherefore, the new salary is \\(\\boxed{10200}\\).",
